/T (Text Field51)
/Rect [ 33.451 59.286 603.637 645.305 ]
/F 4
/V (Based on the available evidence\054 one colony\055like artifact was observed on ScanC\057O CGS E001309 S1 11MAY2026 in ISO 5 BSC E001309 on the date of testing \05011 May 2026\051\056 However\054 the observation could not be confirmed as a viable microbial CFU because no growth was obtained following inoculation onto fresh media\056 Therefore\054 the observation represents a nonviable or non\055microbial artifact\054 including a potential artifact associated with agar preparation or the agar\055pouring process\056\012\012Even if the observed artifact had represented a viable CFU\054 it would appear to be an isolated event\056 This assessment is supported by the absence of microbial recovery from Clea S\056 Garza\047s personnel\055monitoring plates on the date before testing \05008 May 2026\051\054 the date of testing \05011 May 2026\051\054 and the date after testing \05012 May 2026\051\073 the absence of growth from BSC E001309 surface samples collected on the date before testing \05009 May 2026\051 and the date after testing \05012 May 2026\051\073 and the absence of growth from ISO 5 settling plates throughout the bracketing period\056\012\012Although active\055air monitoring recovered 2 CFU \050Gram\055positive cocci and Gram\055positive pleomorphic rods\051 in the surrounding area of Room 117 during the week of testing \05007 May 2026\051\054 this recovery occurred outside the ISO 5 critical environment of BSC E001309\056 Furthermore\054 the ISO 5 Surface S1 observation yielded no growth upon subculture and was confirmed as a non\055viable artifact\056 Therefore\054 a microbiological relationship between the ISO 5 surface artifact and the cleanroom active\055air recovery cannot be established\056\012\012The negative ISO 5 settling\054 personnel\054 and bracketing surface monitoring results demonstrate that the BSC E001309 critical environment remained in a state of control\056 The available data do not support migration\054 persistence\054 or recurrence of contamination within ISO 5 BSC E001309\056 Collectively\054 the evidence supports that the recovery was an isolated\054 transient\054 and non\055recurring event\054 while established cleaning\054 disinfection\054 and aseptic controls remained effective\056\012\012Accordingly\054 no systemic environmental control deficiencies were identified\054 and no additional corrective or preventive actions are warranted at this time beyond continued routine environmental monitoring and adherence to approved cleaning\054 disinfection\054 and aseptic procedures\056)
/Type /Annot
/Subtype /Widget
/M (D\07220250930131345\05506\04700\047)
